Whisper: the Rust build configuration leaves out the update channel unless the crash reporter is built

What: the generated Rust build configuration (mozbuild crate, buildconfig.rs) carries
MOZ_UPDATE_CHANNEL only when the crash reporter is built; the crash reporter's
crash_helper_common is the only Rust code that reads it.
Why: almost all of Gecko's Rust code depends on the mozbuild crate, so a different
update channel made every crate compile anew. Whisper builds no crash reporter, and
Whisper Canary differs from Whisper in its update channel; without the channel in
this file both editions compile the same Rust code and share one compiler cache, so a
canary build takes as long as a release build from a warm cache.
---
diff --git a/build/rust/mozbuild/generate_buildconfig.py b/build/rust/mozbuild/generate_buildconfig.py
--- a/build/rust/mozbuild/generate_buildconfig.py
+++ b/build/rust/mozbuild/generate_buildconfig.py
@@ -156,7 +156,12 @@
     # Used by toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common
     output.write(generate_string("MOZ_APP_ID"))
     output.write(generate_string("MOZ_CRASHREPORTER_URL"))
-    output.write(generate_string("MOZ_UPDATE_CHANNEL"))
+    # Whisper: only the crash reporter's Rust code reads the update channel, and Whisper
+    # builds no crash reporter. Without it here, every crate that depends on this one
+    # (most of Gecko's Rust code) compiles the same for Whisper and Whisper Canary, so
+    # both share one compiler cache.
+    if buildconfig.substs.get("MOZ_CRASHREPORTER"):
+        output.write(generate_string("MOZ_UPDATE_CHANNEL"))
 
     # NSS shared libraries the megazord and rusttests link against. The list lives
     # in mozbuild.nss_libs so that the libsForTests packaging action can use the
